  "habitat": "Pairs and small flocks in waterside grass and reeds, vleis and other marshy ground, and cultivated fields.",
  "summary": "A common resident. Both sexes have barring on a yellowish background, an orange undertail, a red rump and a red bill and face mask. The male’s orange breast is variable and sometimes absent, and he also has a red breast-patch and red vent. The upper parts are grey-brown. The immature is like the female but has a black bill. The call is a quiet metallic tinkling, often in flight. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
